    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0206" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Salt Funds/127</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain (Mellon) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 174</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-24">June 24, 1932</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        2.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith a copy
                    of a statement of views, set forth in a letter to me from Sir John Simon,
                    regarding the recent developments in the Manchurian Salt Gabelle, referred to in
                    the Department’s telegraphic instruction No. 156, May 27, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d117-f1"/> and my telegram No. 189, May 31, 11 a.m. I have been
                    informally advised by Sir John that he has delayed forwarding me the enclosed
                    statement until he had read the State Department’s memorandum regarding evidence
                    of Japanese initiative in the creation and practical control of the new
                    administration of the State of Manchukuo<anchor n="73" xml:id="d117-f2"/> (See
                    Department’s confidential instruction No. 51, May 31, 1932<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d117-f3"/>), the contents of which, however, he has stated, in his
                    opinion, do not affect the conclusions he has formulated in his note to me.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>(For the Ambassador)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray
                            Atherton</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d117-a1.xml" xpointer="d117-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
